+/* GFX803 VA-recycling workaround: a freed VA is withheld from the aperture
+ * free-list until FMM_REUSE_QUEUE_MAX further frees have occurred, so a hot
+ * address is never handed straight back to the next same-size malloc. Mirrors
+ * the proven ring-of-distinct-buffers result (harness 0/52). Length-bounded
+ * (not alloc-counted) so it is O(1) per op and self-limiting for every
+ * aperture regardless of which alloc paths fire -- an alloc-counted delay can
+ * grow unboundedly on apertures whose alloc path doesn't bump the counter.
+ */
+#define FMM_REUSE_QUEUE_MAX 64
+
